<title>NETHERLANDS: TABLE-Unilever Q2 guilder net profit rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Unilever Q2 guilder net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>(in billions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per share (guilders)		29.64  vs  3.35</p>
<p>    Net profit/constant exchange rates   7.72  vs  0.94</p>
<p>    Ditto excl chemicals sale profit     1.37  vs  ----</p>
<p>    Net profit/current exchange rates    8.31  vs  0.94</p>
<p>    Ditto excl chemicals sale profit     1.48  vs  ----</p>
<p>    Turnover				    23.13  vs  22.81</p>
<p>    Operating profit			   2.32  vs  1.77</p>
<p>    Operating profit before exceptionals 2.32  vs  2.00</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			    10.10  vs  1.60</p>
<p>    Ditto excl chemicals sale profit     2.19  vs  ----</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit on chemicals sale     7.92  vs  ----</p>
<p>    Tax					    0.76  vs  0.61</p>
<p>    Tax on chemicals sale profit	   1.50  vs  ----</p>
<p>NOTES -- Anglo Dutch consumer products group Unilever was expected  by analysts to report a second quarter net profit from normal operations  of 1.03 to 1.38 billion guilders.</p>
<p>Unilever said second-quarter and first-half results included provisional  profit on sale of its specialty chemicals business to Britain's ICI.</p>
<p>Before taxes this amounted to 7,916 million guilders at constant 1996  exchange rates or 8,639 million guilders at exchange rates prevailing  on July 8, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
